{
  "suite": "switch-measured-state",
  "description": "Reinterprets a weight as a pre- or post-cooking measurement, converting it so it still describes the same food: multiply by the yield going to \"cooked\", divide coming back to \"raw\" — the same direction convention as apply-method-change branch 1, so the two compose without a sign error. A row already in the requested state is returned untouched rather than converted twice, which is load-bearing: a toggle re-emitting its current value is normal, and without the guard every such event would rescale the weight again. The yield comes from resolveYieldFactor, so a raw method and absent Knowledge data both give factor 1.",
